// The Mirror Pool (Pool_2; character-bibles.md §5). Marrow's one echo in Act 2: a grey chick in the reflection and
// not on the bank. It says back Wren's own last chosen line, in her words. Nothing else. Marrow's lines are copies;
// the #echo tag keeps localisation identical.

title: MirrorPool_Marrow
---
<<if has_flag("marrow.seen_in_pool")>>
    Pool: Only Wren in the water now, in colour. #still #line:0e22e4b
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Pool: Water flat as paper. Wren in it, in colour. #line:08183b6
Pool: Behind her, in the water, a grey chick. On the bank behind her, nothing. #line:0408f62
-> Who's there? #line:0fd34b9
    Marrow: Who's there? #echo:wren #line:0780524
    <<voice surveyor greyfold>>
-> You're not on the bank. #line:016f4b3
    Marrow: Not on the bank. #echo:wren #line:0a74d6f
    <<voice warden greyfold>>
-> ... #line:0b84aa0
    Marrow: ... #echo:wren #line:047a771
    <<voice drift greyfold>>
Pool: A ripple. The chick is gone. The water shows only her. #line:02c17e2
<<flag marrow.seen_in_pool 1>>
===
